    "doomIndexInputSummary": "OpenAI launches Dots, its bubbly agentic avatar. Dots are meant to operate independent of any specific hardware or interface, pursuing user-defined goals continuously in the background with minimal oversight. AI OpenAI OpenAI DevDay OpenAI’s Dots Are Always-On AI Agents—and Its Answer to Meta’s Muse. These cute agents are designed to connect to your apps and tackle multistep tasks. Gear Gear / Gear News and Events OpenAI launches Dots, its Muse competitor. Like Muse, OpenAI’s Dots are represented by cute, customizable avatars. | Image: OpenAI OpenAI is responding to Meta's buzzy Muse AI with agentic helpers of its own: Dots. During its DevDay keynote on Tuesday, OpenAI announced that Dots will serve as always-on AI assistants that can \"do nearly anything\" across connected apps in the background while learning your preferences over time. The company's capable GPT-6 Astra model powers Dots, which use their own cloud computer to access a web browser and more than 4,000 supported apps. You can interact with a Dot through a text-message-like interface that's similar to the one offered by Muse, as well as hop on a voice call with it from ChatGPT on the web, desktop, or mobile. Dots ca … Read the full story at The Verge. OpenAI is responding to Meta's buzzy Muse AI with agentic helpers of its own: Dots. During its DevDay keynote on Tuesday, OpenAI announced that Dots will serve as always-on AI assistants that can \"do nearly anything\" across connected apps in the background while learning your preferences over time. The company's capable GPT-6 Astra model powers […] OpenAI Dots has its own little guy mascots to rival Meta Muse. OpenAI’s new Dots are customizable AI agents designed to learn how you work and keep working toward your goals."
